<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mirandola</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mirandola is a town in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modena">Modena</a> in Emilia-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romagna">Romagna</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, on the plain north of Modena. From the 14th century it was ruled by the Pico family as a fortified lordship, later a principality and duchy, until it was sold to the Este dukes of Modena in 1710. The town was badly damaged by the earthquakes of 2012.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mirandola.jpg" alt="Mirandola" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Boardvital111 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mirandola1.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
